      "text": "11 MR. MOOPPAN: Well, what I'm suggesting is\n12 twofold. First, the act of supervision is a fairly\n13 rigorous standard and I am sure the FTC would have told\n14 you that if you had asked them that question precisely.\n15 And I'm saying that it \u00ad\u00ad the issue here isn't whether\n16 these people will be unsupervised. The question is who\n17 will determine what level of supervision. And the\n18 question is whether the state should decide that a lower\n19 level of supervision is the appropriate one, balancing\n20 expertise versus the risk of conflicts of interests."
